The screen shows LeetCode 32: Longest Valid Parentheses. Return the length of the longest contiguous well-formed substring. A stack tracks unmatched opening parentheses and the boundary before a valid substring.

```javascript
function solve(s) {
  const stack = [-1];
  let best = 0;

  for (let i = 0; i < s.length; i++) {
    if (s[i] === '(') {
      stack.push(i);
    } else {
      stack.pop();
      if (stack.length === 0) {
        stack.push(i);
      } else {
        best = Math.max(best, i - stack[stack.length - 1]);
      }
    }
  }

  return best;
}
```

Call `solve(s)` with a parentheses string; it returns a number, including 0 for an empty string. Time: O(n). Space: O(n).

