The screen shows LeetCode 84: Largest Rectangle in Histogram. Use a monotonic stack of bar indices; when a shorter bar appears, calculate the largest rectangle for each taller bar removed from the stack.

```javascript
function solve(heights) {
  const stack = [];
  let best = 0;
  const n = heights.length;

  for (let i = 0; i <= n; i++) {
    const height = i === n ? 0 : heights[i];

    while (stack.length > 0 &&
           heights[stack[stack.length - 1]] > height) {
      const index = stack.pop();
      const left = stack.length > 0
        ? stack[stack.length - 1]
        : -1;
      const width = i - left - 1;
      best = Math.max(best, heights[index] * width);
    }

    if (i < n) stack.push(i);
  }

  return best;
}
```

Call `solve([2, 1, 5, 6, 2, 3])` to get `10`; an empty array returns `0`. Each index is pushed and popped at most once, so time is O(n) and auxiliary space is O(n).

