The screen shows LeetCode 33: Search in Rotated Sorted Array. Use binary search: one half is always sorted, so check whether the target lies in that half and discard the other half.

```javascript
function solve(nums, target) {
  let left = 0;
  let right = nums.length - 1;

  while (left <= right) {
    const mid = left + Math.floor((right - left) / 2);
    if (nums[mid] === target) return mid;

    if (nums[left] <= nums[mid]) {
      if (nums[left] <= target && target < nums[mid]) {
        right = mid - 1;
      } else {
        left = mid + 1;
      }
    } else {
      if (nums[mid] < target && target <= nums[right]) {
        left = mid + 1;
      } else {
        right = mid - 1;
      }
    }
  }

  return -1;
}
```

Call `solve(nums, target)` directly; it returns the index or `-1`. Time: O(log n). Extra space: O(1).

